0..79 Comment "//! Located judgements over the seat exchange: an operator dispatches work to a"
80..158 Comment "//! seat, the seat works where it stands, and what comes back is a report or a"
159..237 Comment "//! handle to one. The judgement `M : A @ w` reads a term at a world; `A at w`"
238..314 Comment "//! is a handle to a value at `w`, `hold` makes one at the current world and"
315..389 Comment "//! `let x at w` opens one at `w`; `migrate [w] { M }` runs `M` at `w` and"
390..439 Comment "//! spends one capability `cap_w` the entry holds"
440..521 Comment "//! [Vii-2007-typesafe_distributed_programming_ml5], § 3: `get`, `hold`, `leta`."
522..597 Comment "//! Only what is mobile and open comes back: a `mobile type` component of a"
598..651 Comment "//! sealed signature says its representation crosses."
652..655 Comment "//!"
656..716 Comment "//! - cites: [Vii-2007-typesafe_distributed_programming_ml5]"
717..720 Comment "//!"
721..888 Comment "//! [Vii-2007-typesafe_distributed_programming_ml5]: https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-78663-4_9 \"Murphy, Crary and Harper, Type-Safe Distributed Programming with ML5\""
890..964 Comment "// The seat\'s protocol and its messages, sealed, its report marked mobile."
